WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.040
One of the best lines in "Wakanda Forever"&nbsp;
wasn't even in the script. Here's the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.000
behind the improvised moment fans&nbsp;
can't get enough of. Spoilers ahead.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.540
The sequel to one of Marvel's most&nbsp;
successful movies, "Black Panther:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:17.760
Wakanda Forever" is already setting records of its&nbsp;
own, having broken records for a November opening.

00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:22.080
Set in the wake of King T'Challa's death,&nbsp;
which mirrors the real-life death of his actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.040
Chadwick Boseman, the movie explores&nbsp;
how that loss affects those who were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.340
closest to the late monarch. That&nbsp;
means "Wakanda Forever" functions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.840
a lot like an ensemble film, despite its&nbsp;
central character arc belonging to Shuri.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.100
For instance, actor Winston Duke gets&nbsp;
a lot more screen time as M'Baku,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.540
ruler of the mountain-dwelling Jabari&nbsp;
Tribe. M'Baku's role is much expanded in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.140
"Wakanda Forever" compared to the first&nbsp;
"Black Panther," and he's become much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.280
more connected to the rest of Wakanda, even&nbsp;
holding sessions with the kingdom's elders.

00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:56.340
But while M'Baku may have softened a bit, he's&nbsp;
still the intimidating wall of muscle fans know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:01.500
and love. Though his gruffness belies kindness&nbsp;
and humor underneath, it's still a lot of fun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.940
to watch M'Baku towering over everyone around&nbsp;
him and throwing his weight around. Some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.560
the most memorable lines in the film belong to&nbsp;
him. You could even call him a scene stealer.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.700
"I bet you could."

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:13.980
"But no."

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.720
In fact, Duke came up with a few of those&nbsp;
lines himself. The actor took to Twitter to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.040
reveal at least one fan-favorite line that&nbsp;
wasn't in the script. In a post on Twitter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.820
Duke revealed that the moment when&nbsp;
M'Baku, using a carrot as a pointer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:30.780
calls Okoye a "bald-headed&nbsp;
demon" was, in fact, improvised.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.620
As Duke explained, part of his role in&nbsp;
"Wakanda Forever" was to act as comic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.000
relief in tense situations, and that aspect&nbsp;
of the role led him to come up with some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.220
M'Baku's dialogue. Duke wrote in his tweet,

00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:54.840
It's true that M'Baku's role in the film goes a&nbsp;
long way to diffuse the heavy atmosphere hanging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.980
over the proceedings. Few other characters&nbsp;
in "Wakanda Forever" are afforded many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:04.200
opportunities to express their comedic sides,&nbsp;
so M'Baku's funniest lines help to balance out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.364
the movie's darker tones. Even if the character&nbsp;
isn't aware he's being humorous, Duke sure is.

00:02:09.364 --> 00:02:13.560
But Duke's tweet implies that other M'Baku&nbsp;
dialogue across the film was also his own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.920
improvisational deviation from the&nbsp;
script, thus raising the question:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.940
which other lines did Duke come up&nbsp;
with? That mystery is sure to prompt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.560
at least some fans to pay extra attention&nbsp;
to M'Baku's dialogue on a second viewing.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.460
Fans of "Wakanda Forever" were excited&nbsp;
to learn that Winston Duke improvised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.120
his "bald-headed demon" line from the&nbsp;
film. In response to the actor's tweet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.900
revealing that bit of behind-the-scenes&nbsp;
lore, his replies were filled with fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.934
who expressed how much they had loved his&nbsp;
performance and that line in particular.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:42.000
One fan posted,

00:02:45.553 --> 00:02:50.580
Others were even more hyperbolic, with another&nbsp;
fan receiving hundreds of likes for posting,

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.340
"Wakanda Forever" won't be the last&nbsp;
fans see of M'Baku. The end of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:06.060
film implies that he will take over as&nbsp;
the new king of Wakanda, at least for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.220
the time being. Whenever the MCU returns to&nbsp;
Wakanda, M'Baku is almost sure to be there.

